<article class="env-definition" id="010F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/010F">Definition <span data-tag="010F">12.5.9</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $i : A \to B$ and $q : B \to C$ be morphisms of $\mathcal{A}$ such that $0 \to A \to B \to C \to 0$ is a short exact sequence. We say the short exact sequence is <em>split</em> if there exist morphisms $j : C \to B$ and $p : B \to A$ such that $(B, i, j, p, q)$ is the direct sum of $A$ and $C$. </p>
</article>